        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Valance of yellow silk damask with patterns of stylised, curved and geometric shapes. Applied cut silk velvet ribbon with two bands which follow the contours of the scalloped edges. Woven yellow silk braid with fringe at the bottom. Lining of yellow and white striped ribbed silk with a selvedge at the top. The braid at the top edge is missing. Label attached with '30511B' written on it."@en , "Valance of silk damask, made in France, ca. 1860-1885."@en ;
